# =============================================================================
# Vancouver Art Thieves — Server environment variables
# =============================================================================
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Copy it to `.env` (gitignored) to configure the server:
#
#     copy server\.env.example server\.env
#
# The server loads `.env` automatically at startup via dotenv
# (see `import 'dotenv/config'` in src/index.ts).
#
# Precedence: variables already set in your shell/terminal take priority over
# the values in this file (dotenv never overwrites existing environment vars).
#
# Run modes:
#   DB_DRIVER=sqlite  -> SQLite database + uploads/ folder
#   DB_DRIVER=postgres -> PostgreSQL database + uploads/ folder
#   DB_DRIVER=memory  -> no database, no uploads/; everything is ephemeral
#   Shortcut          -> npm run dev:memory (sets PERSIST=false)
#
# See ENV.md (repo root) for the full reference.

# --- Persistence ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Select memory, sqlite, or postgres. The default remains SQLite for local use.
# DB_DRIVER=sqlite

# Legacy switch: PERSIST=false still selects the in-memory backend when DB_DRIVER
# is not set. Prefer DB_DRIVER=memory for new environments.
# PERSIST=false

# Alternative to PERSIST=false: set to 1 to force in-memory mode regardless.
# DB_IN_MEMORY=1

# Location of the SQLite database file (when DB_DRIVER=sqlite).
# Default: <server>/data/vat.db
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/vat.db

# PostgreSQL connection string (when DB_DRIVER=postgres).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/art_thieves

# Optional PostgreSQL migration directory.
# POSTGRES_MIGRATIONS_DIR=./drizzle-postgres

# Folder containing the generated Drizzle migrations (persistent mode only).
# Default: <server>/drizzle
# MIGRATIONS_DIR=./drizzle

# Folder where uploaded game photos are stored (persistent mode only).
# Default: <server>/uploads
# UPLOADS_DIR=./uploads

# --- HTTP ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the server listens on.
# Default: 3001
# PORT=3001
